The origin of ultrahigh energy cosmic rays (UHECRs; ECR≳1E_{\mathrm{CR}}\gtrsim 1 EeV) remains an unresolved question in astroparticle physics. Spectrum, composition, and anisotropy measurements of UHECRs indicate they are predominantly extragalactic and composed of heavy nuclei at the highest energies [28, 53, 44]. However, due to deflections in Galactic and extragalactic magnetic fields [56, 26, 6], source identification remains a challenge.

